  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Given an array of NNN non-negative integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​. In one operation, you can increase **any one** of the elements by 111.\n\nFind the **minimum** number of operations needed to make the XOR of all elements (A1⊕A2⊕…⊕ANA_1 \\oplus A_2 \\oplus \\ldots \\oplus A_NA1​⊕A2​⊕…⊕AN​) equal to 000. Here ⊕\\oplus⊕ denotes the bitwise XOR operation.\n\n\nInput Format\nThe first line of input contains one integer TTT - the number of test cases. Descriptions of TTT test cases follow.\n\n\nThe first line of each test case contains one integer NNN - the size of the array. The second line of each test case contains NNN integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ - the elements of the array.\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, print one number - the **minimum** number of operations required to make the array XOR equal to 000. It can be shown that it is always possible.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\le T \\le 1001≤T≤100",
      "2≤N≤1062 \\le N \\le 10^{6}2≤N≤106",
      "∑N≤106\\sum N \\le 10^{6}∑N≤106",
      "0≤Ai&lt;2600 \\le A_i \\lt 2^{60}0≤Ai​&lt;260",
      "Subtasks",
      "**Subtask 1 (10 points):** 2≤N≤52 \\le N \\le 52≤N≤5, Ai&lt;24A_i \\lt 2^{4}Ai​&lt;24",
      "**Subtask 2 (20 points):** 2≤N≤1002 \\le N \\le 1002≤N≤100, ∑N≤1000\\sum N \\le 1000∑N≤1000, Ai&lt;27A_i \\lt 2^{7}Ai​&lt;27",
      "**Subtask 3 (10 points):** 2≤N≤72 \\le N \\le 72≤N≤7, ∑N≤100\\sum N \\le 100∑N≤100, Ai&lt;260A_i \\lt 2^{60}Ai​&lt;260",
      "**Subtask 4 (10 points):** 2≤N≤132 \\le N \\le 132≤N≤13, ∑N≤100\\sum N \\le 100∑N≤100, Ai&lt;260A_i \\lt 2^{60}Ai​&lt;260",
      "**Subtask 5 (25 points):** 2≤N≤10002 \\le N \\le 10002≤N≤1000, ∑N≤10 000\\sum N \\le 10\\,000∑N≤10000, Ai&lt;230A_i \\lt 2^{30}Ai​&lt;230",
      "**Subtask 6 (15 points):** 2≤N≤1062 \\le N \\le 10^{6}2≤N≤106, ∑N≤106\\sum N \\le 10^{6}∑N≤106, Ai&lt;230A_i \\lt 2^{30}Ai​&lt;230",
      "**Subtask 7 (10 points):** Original constraints"
    ],
