    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n3\n3 4 5\n4\n5 3 0 7\n3\n2 3 1\n5\n7 7 7 7 7",
        "output": "2\n1\n0\n9",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Increase A3A_3A3​ twice by using two operations. Thus, the array becomes [3,4,7][3, 4, 7][3,4,7]. The XOR of all elements of the array is 3⊕4⊕7=03\\oplus 4\\oplus 7 = 03⊕4⊕7=0. It can be shown that the XOR of all elements cannot be made equal to 000 using less than 222 operations.\nTest case 222: Use one operation to increase A3A_3A3​ by 111. Thus, the array becomes [5,3,1,7][5, 3, 1, 7][5,3,1,7]. The XOR of all elements of the array is 5⊕3⊕1⊕7=05\\oplus 3\\oplus 1\\oplus 7 = 05⊕3⊕1⊕7=0. It can be shown that the XOR of all elements cannot be made equal to 000 using less than 111 operation.\nTest case 333: The XOR of all elements is already 000. Thus, we require 000 operations."
      }
    ]
